{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734722",
      "title": "Updating State Based On Previous State",
      "sourceHash": "c86e9f5699989bf39553def2c460850b75728224aaa0e0b5c63267101dc172f7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 4.59,
          "en": "So we're gathering that post data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.59,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "How can we now add that as a post to a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 11.04,
          "en": "of posts that should then be output dynamically here instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.04,
          "end": 14.01,
          "en": "of outputting this hard coded post here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "Well, in the end, again, by using what we already know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 20.763,
          "en": "plus two new concepts or features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 25.23,
          "en": "In the end we have to get this post data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.23,
          "end": 29.1,
          "en": "from the new post component to the post's list component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 31.92,
          "en": "And there we then should manage some state which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.92,
          "end": 34.35,
          "en": "in the end manages a list of posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.35,
          "end": 37.65,
          "en": "And whenever that list changes we wanna update the list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.65,
          "end": 39.003,
          "en": "for outputting down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 44.67,
          "en": "Therefore, we can useState here and import useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.67,
          "end": 47.4,
          "en": "from React in the post list component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.4,
          "end": 50.733,
          "en": "and pass an MT array as an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.6,
          "end": 56.6,
          "en": "And that then should be our posts array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.06,
          "end": 60.033,
          "en": "with a setPosts state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.56,
          "end": 64.02,
          "en": "So the idea is that here we manage a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.02,
          "end": 66.72,
          "en": "of posts and that list should be edited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.72,
          "end": 69.3,
          "en": "whenever we submit a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.3,
          "end": 71.97,
          "en": "So therefore, we also must add a function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.97,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "in posts list, which adds a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 77.97,
          "en": "And that could be the addPostHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.97,
          "end": 81.18,
          "en": "and I name it addPostHandler, because in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.18,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "again it should be triggered whenever the form is submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 85.07300000000001,
          "en": "in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.37,
          "end": 88.99,
          "en": "Now here we could expect to get some postData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.21000000000001,
          "end": 94.45,
          "en": "and then we wanna update our post state with set posts here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 100.17,
          "en": "and in the end, pass a new post object to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.17,
          "end": 103.5,
          "en": "Now for that, what we could do is pass a new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.5,
          "end": 108.12,
          "en": "as a new state value to set posts and then add post data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.12,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "as a new value to that array and to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 115.5,
          "en": "that any potentially existing posts aren't lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.5,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "We could use this spread operator, a default operator built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 123.9,
          "en": "into JavaScript to spread our existing posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.9,
          "end": 125.633,
          "en": "into this new array of posts so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.633,
          "end": 128.55,
          "en": "that we add this new post as the first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.55,
          "end": 131.523,
          "en": "in this array and the existing posts come thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "This is not optimal, but it will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 138.63,
          "en": "So now we just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 141.84,
          "en": "that the addPostHandler is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "as the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "For that, we can pass this addPostHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 151.77,
          "en": "with help of a prop to the new post component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.77,
          "end": 156.69,
          "en": "So we could add a prop called onAddPost and set the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.69,
          "end": 160.353,
          "en": "of that prop to the addPostHandler function we just added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162.06,
          "end": 164.19,
          "en": "And in that the new post component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.19,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "we can now use the onAddPost prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 169.74,
          "en": "again using the same mechanism we've used over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 173.01,
          "en": "and over again to accept that prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 176.11,
          "en": "and destructure it from this props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.09,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "and in submit handler before calling on cancel,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "we can now call on at post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 186.27,
          "en": "Since this again is a prop yielding a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.27,
          "end": 188.13,
          "en": "and passing the post data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.13,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "to this function and this function that is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 195.783,
          "en": "in the end is this addPostHandler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.62,
          "end": 199.92000000000002,
          "en": "So this will now add this post to this array of posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.92000000000002,
          "end": 202.93,
          "en": "But as I mentioned, this code here isn't ideal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 207.87,
          "en": "because there is a rule if you update state and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.87,
          "end": 212.16,
          "en": "that new state is based on that previous state value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 212.16,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "as it's the case here where the new state is based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 220.65,
          "en": "on the existing posts you should actually pass a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 220.65,
          "end": 224.55,
          "en": "to set posts for example, an arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 227.7,
          "en": "And this function here will be called automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 227.7,
          "end": 231.183,
          "en": "by React whenever you call set posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 232.77,
          "end": 234.78,
          "en": "And this function will automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.78,
          "end": 238.62,
          "en": "receive the current state snapshot, so the existing posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 238.62,
          "end": 241.5,
          "en": "and you should then return the new state value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 241.5,
          "end": 242.79,
          "en": "where you could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.79,
          "end": 247.623,
          "en": "again add your post data and spread the existing posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.64,
          "end": 251.46,
          "en": "Now this looks very similar to what we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 251.46,
          "end": 254.67,
          "en": "but it's the technically better way of updating your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.67,
          "end": 258.33,
          "en": "if it depends on the previous state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.33,
          "end": 262.38,
          "en": "The reason for data is that internally React does actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.38,
          "end": 266.31,
          "en": "not execute your state updating functions instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 266.31,
          "end": 269.31,
          "en": "At least it's not guaranteed that it will do so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 269.31,
          "end": 272.82,
          "en": "But it schedules those state updates and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 272.82,
          "end": 275.58,
          "en": "in case you have multiple state updates after each other,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 278.04,
          "en": "you could potentially update your state based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 280.32,
          "en": "on some old state or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.32,
          "end": 282.39,
          "en": "And therefore, this way is a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 282.39,
          "end": 285.03,
          "en": "of making sure that React ensures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 285.03,
          "end": 287.34000000000003,
          "en": "that you get the latest correct state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 287.34000000000003,
          "end": 289.44,
          "en": "for this state update even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 293.01,
          "en": "if you have multiple pending state updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 293.01,
          "end": 295.08,
          "en": "So therefore, it's this simple rule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 295.08,
          "end": 297.6,
          "en": "If the new state depends on the old state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 297.6,
          "end": 299.73,
          "en": "then you should use this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 299.73,
          "end": 301.02,
          "en": "for updating the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 301.02,
          "end": 303.863,
          "en": "You get the old state automatically, you can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 303.863,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "and you should return the new state then as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 309.72,
          "en": "And you can use the old state if you need to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.72,
          "end": 311.61,
          "en": "as it's the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.61,
          "end": 314.76,
          "en": "And this does not just apply if your state is an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.76,
          "end": 318.412,
          "en": "but whenever your new state depends on the old state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 318.412,
          "end": 321.93,
          "en": "And with that, we're managing this list of posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 321.93,
          "end": 324.09,
          "en": "How can we now output it down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.09,
          "end": 328.773,
          "en": "and render one post component per post item in this array?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}